From d35d2a3652cd9c62be76b3de79daed764194aba7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:44:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 234/239] Part: solidFromMesh and filletMeshSolid for solids
 made from STL

Part.solidFromMesh(mesh, tolerance, refine=True, fillHoles=20, report=False) repairs
the mesh before making the shape (points closer than the tolerance merged,
duplicated and degenerated facets removed, orientation made consistent, small holes
filled), sews, turns an inverted solid outside out, merges coplanar triangles into
faces (UnifySameDomain with the tolerance, fixed and checked against the volume)
and reports repairs and problems (open, non-manifold, self-intersecting).  Fewer,
real faces make booleans and sections faster and steadier; the doc string says to
use a fuzzy value (common(b, tol), findInterferences(tolerance=tol)).

Part.filletMeshSolid(shape_or_mesh, radius, edges=None, minAngle=30) rounds the
sharp straight edges of such a solid (prismatic parts); edges where the fillet fails
stay sharp and are reported, with a time limit for the one-by-one fallback.  Curved
regions of a mesh (narrow facets) are not rounded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
